   KEY: A PORTABILITY TEST THAT PASSES MAY HAVE RESOLVED BACK INTO THE AUTHOR'S OWN TREE.
        Make the resolver PRINT WHAT IT RESOLVED -- a rc=0 from a foreign checkout is not
        evidence of portability unless the path it used is in the transcript.
        (This is c50's portability law one layer down: c50 said the test must run from a checkout
         that is not yours; this says the test must also READ from it.)
